SELECT sift.scope_create('dup_copy', 'facts', 'dim_a_id', 'dup_pairs', 'scope_id');
ERROR:  scope_create: table "public.dup_pairs" has no unique index on (dim_a_id, scope_id)
DETAIL:  A scope relation holds each (member, scope key) pair once: a duplicate pair would give a row two copies in one key.
CONTEXT:  PL/pgSQL function sift.scope_create(text,regclass,name,regclass,name,name[],boolean,name,name) line 39 at RAISE
